oundations II, the second step of the journey towards university-level math." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1009 "Solidify your arithmetic, learn about variables and graphs, level up your algebra, and learn the essentials of geometry." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1012 113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1013 "MF1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1014 #uuid "042e624c-a46d-509f-a48e-61bd6d3e082c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1031 "Volumes of Right Rectangular Prisms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1033 2404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049294 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "ea592b1e-e897-594c-ab88-937718bccd2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1031 "Understanding Volume Using Unit Cubes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1033 2403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050338 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "41041814-a377-5adb-96e1-952df5762433" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186188300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186188301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186188302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1031 "Units of Area and Volume" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1033 3872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050792 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "675d7c57-7050-5b6e-8c59-6608d72d4947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142704 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142704 #edb/ref 1071 "If each cube represents one cubic unit, what is the volume of the figure?\n\n![](images/54/544b5a74ce1d8c5545d32df665df7d10ba4853cdf166ca02a3a03b46e2a97259.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142704 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c041baf7-07b4-5c1a-969d-4324a3417f92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142704 #edb/ref 1074 "The figure consists of $10$ cubes.\n\n![](images/df/dfa571cbacb1f3e06ce70e05c127239cb159fdbc9adbd937df6120a5f214b120.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume is $10$ cubic units." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142705 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2148" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142705 #edb/ref 1071 "If each cube represents $1$ cubic unit, what is the volume of the figure?\n\n![](images/2e/2e9da7bdc1b3e20a197be4c7e2ab3a64abcbdd78dc16274bc314e73bdc6bd1ce.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142705 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40f45207-a212-5fb2-8c5c-5625e367301f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142705 #edb/ref 1074 "The figure consists of $3$ rows, and each row has $5$ cubes.\n\n![](images/ba/baa53ae50449e9d56821925d9fbe5d2ebf694badd4e1e5e3c604fdcbf698a16f.png)\n\nSo, there are $5 \\times 3 = 15$ cubes in total.\n\nTherefore, the volume of the figure is $15$ cubic units." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142706 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142706 #edb/ref 1071 "An object is assembled as shown below. Given that each small cube represents one cubic unit, what is the volume of the object?\n\n![](images/53/5304eed09b6d029958fbfcce95001c79a8a9dbdd91e7c8ae6eefa7d54db61a75.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142706 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5316b5a3-dec6-5e2c-a14e-ee19c1040916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142706 #edb/ref 1074 "The figure consists of two layers:\n\n- The bottom layer consists of $4$ cubes.\n\n- The top layer consists of $1$ cube.\n\n![](images/4c/4c6372a05b21e7aa9f26717fdbb2cfe47e17d2d17215e9b7411e876b0e6473f5.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume is $4+1=5$ cubic units." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Volume of a Figure by Counting" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186142704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142883 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6057e526-a6a3-562d-b6e5-d72ac184b968" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142884 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142884 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142884 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Volume of a Figure by Multiplying" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142884 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186142705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142884 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "12445ca3-d861-5cf8-98c2-603026cfe199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142885 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142885 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186143398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142885 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Volume of a Figure Containing Multiple Layers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142885 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186142706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186142885 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2ee3dbcf-50d2-542c-9519-fbdcd4ac5b52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186143808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1045 "Understanding Volume Using Unit Cubes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186143803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143033 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "1ea98903-be03-54ee-a4af-ad6a084260e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143803 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143803 #edb/ref 1061 604864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143803 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dbf328d0-e455-5024-ae5a-d1dbd16b32d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143803 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186143995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143804 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143804 #edb/ref 1061 604865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143804 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "14023ba2-9d6a-5179-b29d-c2d1893fc2f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143804 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186142883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143805 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143805 #edb/ref 1061 604868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143805 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95654ea7-6c8d-5f85-93cc-e6eb65a408a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143805 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186142884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143806 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143806 #edb/ref 1061 604871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143806 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9c8e84bb-8ce1-5ca3-9905-45f12e5aed4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143806 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186143996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143807 #edb/ref 1061 604872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143807 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e65cc34b-2b13-5be9-80ab-065730d3bbe1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143807 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186142885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143808 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186143804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143808 #edb/ref 1061 604880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143808 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "14ae82bf-123e-5049-8743-6d3ec50f0915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143808 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186143972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143972 #edb/ref 1064 "We can use metric and customary units to measure volume. \n\nConsider the cube below, whose length, width, and height all equal $1$ centimeter.\n\n![](images/2a/2a87c66750f85974528df85c7956a13a7e3a7982490d22113879ee80881badfb.png)\n\nSince the length, width, and height of this cube all equal $1$ centimeter,  the volume of this cube is $\\mathbf 1$ **cubic centimeter.**\n\nCommonly used metric units of volume are:\n\n- cubic meters\n\n- cubic centimeters\n\n- cubic millimeters\n\nCommonly used customary units of volume are:\n\n- cubic feet\n\n- cubic inches\n\nWe'll learn more about units of volume in future lessons." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143972 #edb/ref 1065 14836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143972 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "12f18b2c-66de-5ce9-af17-3ac954d482bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143972 #edb/ref 1067 "Units of Volume" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143995 #edb/ref 1064 "**Volume** is the amount of space that an object takes up. We can measure volume with **unit cubes**, like the one below.\n\n![](images/a3/a318f6234bdbf014e4cbefbc1add274dbcc37b08f59d93a5fe53c463e962cc86.png)\n\nThese are called unit cubes because each one represents $1$ cubic unit. The volume of a figure is the number of unit cubes that make it up.\n\nFor example, let's find the volume of the figure below:\n\n![](images/12/1215ed078257410d4aab5cff0a58dcbc719c477211bdec8a77b9d10a2ecb5dae.png)\n\nThe figure consists of $2$ cubes. \n\n![](images/4b/4ba5e58d16c4bf9e684590e0280c4ddbd32c5b2c2bbf94412ca77713d9f059b0.png)\n\nTherefore, its volume is $2$ cubic units." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143995 #edb/ref 1065 2000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143995 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a4dc0491-8422-502e-9ecd-f199ce666a9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143995 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143996 #edb/ref 1064 "If a figure has multiple layers, we can find its volume by first finding the volume of each layer and then adding the results.\n\nEach cube in the figure below represents one cubic unit. Let's find its volume.\n\n![](images/54/547a09fed5b5b736b556db4d476f869a68a39528f59d6a5abe505f1fa38260d9.png)\n\nThe figure consists of two layers:\n\n- The bottom layer consists of $2$ cubes.\n\n- The top layer consists of $2$ cubes, too.\n\n![](images/6b/6b7e4ce3ffa821b4263213782bf99a4243f3b844c862e49fcf5181a6f4cdacd2.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume is $2+2=4$ cubic units." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143996 #edb/ref 1065 2001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143996 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a4ba0e39-861d-56ee-a198-e03e2de4bc6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186143996 #edb/ref 1067 "Figures With Multiple Layers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432172 #edb/ref 1080 "$11$ cubic inches" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432172 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432172 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07e75810-7ed0-5d76-9fad-d51b85e81e0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432173 #edb/ref 1080 "$4$ cubic units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432173 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432173 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2823e0d7-82d0-5160-81d6-a3e70a6a7fe9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432174 #edb/ref 1080 "$4$ cubic units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432174 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432174 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f75a191-3f99-5b30-b9fd-bdd56d5dbae2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432175 #edb/ref 1080 "$6$ cubic inches" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432175 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432175 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f775cfe-b42f-568b-b1f0-6032ca161de1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432176 #edb/ref 1080 "$10$ cubic inches" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432176 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432176 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b07fd1f-09f4-5fab-9868-5b695b9dddef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432177 #edb/ref 1080 "$8$ cubic inches" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432177 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432177 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e964b86-655f-5b0f-90cf-94b1ab5e254d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432178 #edb/ref 1080 "$3$ cubic units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432178 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432178 #e